From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vkd3d-shader: the expression vectorizer keeps casts to different types apart

vectorize_exprs merged expressions with the same operation and sources,
whatever their result types: a uint's cast to float and its cast to int are
both HLSL_OP1_CAST, so "int2(gtid.x, 0)" and "gtid.x + 0.5" became one utof
and the texture was indexed with the float's bits -- in a compute shader
every thread but the first wrote out of bounds, i.e. nowhere. Paint.NET 5.2's
compute effects (Auto-Level) came out transparent. Expressions of different
result base types are not vectorized together.
---
--- a/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl_codegen.c
@@ -3912,6 +3912,13 @@
 {
     if (a->op != b->op)
         return false;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_HLSL_VECTORIZE_ANY_TYPE
+    /* wine-sg 9207: the same operation on the same source can still differ in its result type -- a
+     * cast of a uint to float and a cast of it to int are both HLSL_OP1_CAST: merged, the int took the
+     * float's bits (int2(id.x, 0) indexed with utof(id.x), and every thread but the first wrote nowhere) */
+    if (a->node.data_type->e.numeric.type != b->node.data_type->e.numeric.type)
+        return false;
+#endif
 
     for (size_t j = 0; j < HLSL_MAX_OPERANDS; ++j)
     {
